CMD: always gets overridden at the runtime
Entrypoint: it doesn't

CMD provides default arguments to the ENTRYPOINT. If both ENTRYPOINT and CMD are used, ENTRYPOINT specifies the command, and CMD provides default arguments.


FROM ubuntu:22.04
ENTRYPOINT ["python"]
CMD ["app.py"]
ENTRYPOINT ["python"]: Specifies that the main executable is python.
CMD ["app.py"]: Provides default arguments to python, so the full command executed when the container starts is python app.py
